  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and articulation of communities affected by mining to defend their rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to strengthen communities, indigenous peoples and organisations affected by mining in order to defend their individual and collective rights. In a context marked by the climate crisis, the expansion of mining extractivism and the weakening of democracy in Peru, Red Muqui seeks to improve active participation of women, young people and community actors. Through a strategic articulation between the partner institutions of Red Muqui and the communities and populations that they accompany in the territories, the project proposes to recognise alternatives for living well, and to position the demands and proposals of the communities in national and international decision-making spaces.</narrative>
  </description>
